.TH PNDCGN 1 "2025-12-14" "pndcgn v0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pndcgn \- Documentation Generation Tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pndcgn
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fISOURCE_DIR\fR] [\fITARGET_DIR\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pndcgn
is a robust, configurable command-line tool for converting Markdown-based
documentation sources into organized output sets (PDF, HTML, EPUB, DOCX, etc.)
using Pandoc with intelligent caching and resumable runs.
.PP
The tool discovers documentation files in a source directory, converts them
using Pandoc, and organizes the outputs in a structured directory with an
index for easy navigation. It features intelligent caching to avoid regenerating
unchanged files, dry-run mode for previewing operations, and the ability to
resume interrupted runs.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fBSOURCE_DIR\fR
Source directory containing documentation files (default: current directory).
If not provided and running interactively, the tool may use fzf for directory
selection.
.TP
\fBTARGET_DIR\fR
Target directory for generated outputs (default: current directory). Outputs
are placed in \fB\fITARGET_DIR\fR/.pndcgn/\fITYPE\fR-\fIRUN_ID\fR/\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB--type\fR \fITYPE\fR
Output type/format (default: pdf). Supported types include all Pandoc formats:
pdf, html, epub, docx, odt, rtf, and others. See \fBpandoc --list-output-formats\fR
for complete list.
.TP
\fB--dry-run\fR
Preview mode: compute what would be generated without creating output artifacts.
Prints a run ID that can be used with \fB--finalize\fR to execute the plan later.
.TP
\fB--finalize\fR \fIRUN_ID\fR
Finalize a prior dry-run. Validates that inputs and configuration are unchanged
since the dry-run, then generates the outputs. Fails with an error if anything
has changed.
.TP
\fB--resume\fR \fIRUN_ID\fR
Resume an interrupted or partial run. Skips already-processed files and continues
from where it left off. Validates fingerprint to ensure source files haven't changed.
.TP
\fB--force\fR
Bypass cache and regenerate all files, even if they haven't changed.
.TP
\fB--reseed\fR
Re-seed the \fB.pndcgnignore\fR file from current ignore rules (typically
from \fB.gitignore\fR). Useful when ignore patterns have changed.
.TP
\fB--clean\fR \fIRUN_ID\fR [\fIRUN_ID\fR ...]
Remove outputs for one or more specified run IDs. Requires confirmation unless
\fB--yes\fR is used. Validates that output directories contain only pndcgn artifacts.
.TP
\fB--drop\fR
Clear all cache and state data. This removes the entire database and all cached
information. Requires confirmation unless \fB--yes\fR is used.
.TP
\fB--yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts. Required in non-interactive environments (e.g., CI/CD).
.TP
\fB--verbose\fR
Enable verbose output with detailed progress information.
.TP
\fB--quiet\fR, \fB-q\fR
Suppress non-error output. Only errors and warnings are displayed.
.TP
\fB--version\fR, \fB-v\fR
Display version information and exit.
.TP
\fB--help\fR, \fB-h\fR
Display help message and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.SS Ignore Patterns
The tool uses a \fB.pndcgnignore\fR file in the source directory to exclude files
from processing. This file is auto-created on first run by seeding from \fB.gitignore\fR
if present. Patterns follow the same syntax as \fB.gitignore\fR.
.SS TOML Configuration
Optional configuration can be provided via a TOML file. The tool searches for
\fBpndcgn.toml\fR in the following order:
.IP 1. 4
XDG config directory: \fB${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/pndcgn/pndcgn.toml\fR
.IP 2. 4
Source directory root: \fB\fISOURCE_DIR\fR/pndcgn.toml\fR
.PP
The TOML file can specify include patterns, file extensions, and other options.
See the documentation for the complete configuration format.
.SH EXAMPLES
Generate PDFs from the current directory:
.RS
.B pndcgn
.RE
.PP
Generate HTML from a specific source directory:
.RS
.B pndcgn --type html docs/ output/
.RE
.PP
Preview what would be generated:
.RS
.B pndcgn --dry-run
.RE
.PP
Finalize a dry-run:
.RS
.B pndcgn --finalize 01ARZ3NDEKTSV4Y5QH6J7K8M9
.RE
.PP
Resume an interrupted run:
.RS
.B pndcgn --resume 01ARZ3NDEKTSV4Y5QH6J7K8M9
.RE
.PP
Clean up old run outputs:
.RS
.B pndcgn --clean 01ARZ3NDEKTSV4Y5QH6J7K8M9 01ARZ3NDEKTSV4Y5QH6J7K8M0
.RE
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error (e.g., file not found, permission denied, processing failure)
.TP
.B 2
Invalid usage (e.g., unknown option, missing required argument)
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB.pndcgnignore\fR
Ignore patterns file in source directory (auto-created on first run)
.TP
\fBpndcgn.toml\fR
Optional TOML configuration file (in XDG config dir or source directory)
.TP
\fB${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/pndcgn/pndcgn.db\fR
SQLite database storing run history and cache information
.TP
\fB\fITARGET_DIR\fR/.pndcgn/\fITYPE\fR-\fIRUN_ID\fR/\fR
Output directory for generated artifacts
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBNO_COLOR\fR
If set, disables ANSI color output (see https://no-color.org/)
.TP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR
Base directory for user-specific configuration files (default: \fB$HOME/.config\fR)
.TP
\fBXDG_STATE_HOME\fR
Base directory for user-specific state files (default: \fB$HOME/.local/state\fR)
.TP
\fBTERM\fR
Terminal type. If unset or set to "dumb", colors and animations are disabled.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.B pndcgn
requires the following external tools:
.TP
.B pandoc
Document conversion engine (version 2.0+ recommended)
.TP
.B sqlite3
SQLite database engine for state and cache management
.TP
.B curl
Used for downloading sqlite-ulid extension (optional, falls back to Bash-based ULID)
.PP
Optional dependencies:
.TP
.B fzf
Fuzzy finder for interactive directory selection (falls back to current directory if unavailable)
